course: dictionary
lesson: 11036
title: Wealth: money and plenty
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Wealth means a large amount of money, property and things that are worth a lot. Someone with wealth is rich. The clues around the word help you: «The rich fool built bigger barns to store his wealth» tells you the barns held a lot of valuable things.
explain: Wealth has a second meaning, about plenty. A wealth of something is a large amount of it. In «a wealth of ideas», the word means lots of ideas, not money. Ask yourself: is the sentence talking about money, or about a big amount of something?
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «The rich fool built bigger barns to store his lots of valuable things, but died that night.» It still makes sense, so in this sentence wealth means valuable things.
fact: Wealth is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say «great wealth», not «three wealths».
fact: Great wealth means a lot of money and things that are worth a lot.
fact: A wealth of something means a large amount of it, as in «a wealth of information».
fact: «Gōngxǐ fācái» means «wishing you wealth and luck!», the classic New Year wish to grown-ups, and the answer is the same wish back.
fact: Useful phrases: «health and wealth» (two good things to wish for) and «share the wealth» (give some of what you have to others).
exercise: «The rich fool built bigger barns to store his wealth, but died that night.» What does wealth mean here? | *Money and valuable things | Bricks and wood for building | Friends and family | A bad mood
exercise: The library has «a wealth of information». What does a wealth of information mean? | No information at all | A list of rich people | A small, empty box | *A large amount of information
exercise: At New Year, someone says «gōngxǐ fācái» to you. What is a good reply? | *Gōngxǐ fācái, the same wish back | I am sorry, I have no money | Thank you for the book | Goodbye
test: Which word is closest in meaning to wealth? | Silence | Fear | Hunger | *Riches
test: Which sentence uses wealth to mean a large amount of something, not money? | *The team had a wealth of ideas for the school play. | The bakery was short of flour. | The king kept his wealth in gold coins. | The merchant counted his wealth every night.
exam: Ming meets the word wealth and is not sure what it means. What should he do first? | *Read the clues around the word and try his meaning in the sentence | Skip the whole text and never come back | Look up every other word in the sentence | Guess that wealth is the name of a place
